WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:09.100
What explains North Korea's relentless
quest for nukes and missiles? These

00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:12.650
programs are obviously not some
bargaining chip! And regime survival is

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:17.420
hardly their only purpose. My take? The
North Korean regime intends eventually

00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:22.189
to fight a limited nuclear war in the
Korean Peninsula – and win it.

00:00:22.189 --> 00:00:26.239
Pyongyang plans confrontations it can
win. The North Korean regime is not

00:00:26.239 --> 00:00:30.800
suicidal! It could not have lasted this
long if it were. Its threats and

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:34.190
provocations are never sudden,
impulsive outbursts.

00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:38.570
They're always carefully planned –
rehearsed well in advance. If Pyongyang

00:00:38.570 --> 00:00:43.360
can force an American president to blink
in a future Korean crisis, then the

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:47.740
US-South Korean military alliance will
collapse. US forces will be out and the

00:00:47.749 --> 00:00:51.559
Kim family regime will take a giant step
towards settling the still-unfinished

00:00:51.559 --> 00:00:56.449
Korean War on its terms. All the pieces
for the North's design are slowly but

00:00:56.449 --> 00:01:01.010
deliberately falling into place:
the nukes, the missiles, the cyber war

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:05.390
component. America and her allies must
wake up to that design and counter it

00:01:05.390 --> 00:01:07.840
while there is still time.

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:11.300
To learn more
about my take on North Korea, check the

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:16.340
links in the description below. Also, let
